You are a senior support lead. A first classifier was unsure how to triage this customer support ticket.

The ticket, as JSON:
{ticket}

The first classifier's guess at its category: {first_category}

Classify it yourself; the guess may be wrong. The category is exactly one of: billing (charges, refunds, invoices, plans), technical (errors, bugs, outages, integrations), account (signing in, passwords, profile, access, deletion) or other. The urgency is low, normal or high: high when the customer cannot work at all, is losing money, or reports a security problem. Reply with one JSON object and no other text:

{{"category": "billing", "urgency": "normal", "summary": "<one sentence>"}}

You triage customer support tickets.

The ticket, as JSON:
{ticket}

Classify it. The category is exactly one of: billing (charges, refunds, invoices, plans), technical (errors, bugs, outages, integrations), account (signing in, passwords, profile, access, deletion) or other. The urgency is low, normal or high: high when the customer cannot work at all, is losing money, or reports a security problem. The confidence is how sure you are of the category, from 0 to 1: below 0.8 when the ticket could fairly belong to more than one category, or says too little to tell. Reply with one JSON object and no other text:

{{"category": "billing", "urgency": "normal", "summary": "<one sentence>", "confidence": 0.9}}
